<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded empire 1501</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail I was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid dynasty</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and was proclaimed shah in 1501. He made Twelver Shia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> the state religion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, a decision with lasting consequences. His defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at Chaldiran in 1514 set limits to his expansion, but he laid the foundations of the Safavid Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ismail-i.jpg" alt="Ismail I" width="251" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kamāl ud-Dīn Behzād · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shah_Ismail_I_Safavid,_Behzad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
